"""Vendored AWS schemas — committed rather than fetched.

⛔ These are here because their upstream URLs are UNVERSIONED. A `sha256` pinned
against an unversioned URL is a checksum on a moving target: it does not protect
the build, it breaks it on the publisher's schedule. See
//cloudformation/private:extensions.bzl for the measurement that established this.

Refresh deliberately, never automatically:

    curl -fsSL https://schema.cloudformation.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/aws-s3-bucket.json \
      -o cloudformation/private/vendor/aws-s3-bucket.json
    bazel run //cloudformation:update   # regenerates defs.bzl + cfn_types.bzl

and commit the regenerated files in the SAME change — the diff_test gates in
//cloudformation compare against them.
"""

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

exports_files(["aws-s3-bucket.json"])
